┋┋ ━ The text mark
┋┋┋ ━ octant
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $type=str, 1 char
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸆ One of 256 patterns over a 2×4 lattice; one glyph carries a 2×4 patch of the matrix.
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=5.1.2
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=5.1.5
┋┋┋ ━ sextant
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $type=str, 1 char
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸆ One of 64 patterns over a 2×3 lattice; four years older in Unicode, so more fonts have it, and what .txt is drawn on.
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=5.1.2
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=5.1.5
┋┋┋ ━ colour map angle
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $type=float, degrees
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸆ The 28 bits of the digest as degrees, before the warp. What the colour map is indexed at. Not a hue: the hue is this value warped.
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=2.3.1
┋┋┋ ━ shape
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $type=square or circle
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸆ Which of the two glyphs a colour is drawn as, one bit per position from character 16 of the digest. Every colour has both.
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=2.4.1
┋┋┋ ━ colour block
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $type=int, and 3 colour names
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸆ One of the colour map's blocks: a stretch of the circle and the three colours that stand for it. Unordered and unshaped -- it is what the map decides, and nothing more.
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=2.3.11
┋┋┋ ━ the tricolour
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸆ Three of the palette's nine colours, each drawn as a square or a circle, standing for the mark where neither an image nor an escape sequence survives.
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $type=3 of 9 colours
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=2.4.1
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $defines=5.3.1
┋┋┋ ━ arrangement
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸆ The order the three colours are laid out in, from character 15 of the digest.
┊┊┊┊ ┄ ⸖ $type=tuple of 3 int
